// The IndexedDB semantics, once, for every target that can reach IndexedDB.
//
// There are two ways into IndexedDB from MoonBit and they have nothing in
// common. On the `js` backend an `IDBRequest` becomes a `Promise` and
// `Promise::wait()` turns it back into a value. On `wasm-gc` a closure cannot
// cross into JavaScript at all, so the page hands JS a token and JS calls back
// into an export with it.
//
// What they have in common is everything else: implicit directories, the
// `U+FFFF` key bound, a range delete that agrees with the listing, `stat` on a
// directory nobody stored a marker for, `create_dir` walking ancestors. That is
// the same problem twice, so -- following `listing.mbt`, which exists for the
// same reason -- it is solved once here, over a `Conn` seam, in a package with
// no target and no FFI.
//
// The prize is not only the duplication. A `Conn` over a `Map` is a store this
// package can drive under `moon test` on every backend, so the semantics that
// used to be verifiable only in a browser now have unit tests.
import {
  "marianoguerra/sos",
  "moonbitlang/core/json",
}

import {
  "marianoguerra/sos/testing",
} for "test"
